push
prompt pop
string ok_to_proceed
comment Check for the root directory -- if so, turn superuser on.
class(1 2) ignore
[!equal,[!directory],:]
  superuser on
[!else]
  comment Not in the root - check for write access. If we can create
  comment and read from a file, assume we have needed access.
  permanence =?[!pid].[!username].tmp off
  delete =?[!pid].[!username].tmp
  write/l==?[!pid].[!username].tmp test
  string [=?[!pid].[!username].tmp]
  delete =?[!pid].[!username].tmp
  [!equal,[!string],test]
    string ok_to_proceed
  [!else]
    string no_access
  [!end]
[!end]
comment If it's not ok to proceed, describe error and stop.
[!nequal,[!string],ok_to_proceed]
  [!equal,[!string],no_access]
    write
    write Error - [!username] does not have write access to [!directory].
    write ,,,,,,,,,You cannot back up this directory.
    write
  [!end]
[!else]
  comment Check if CLI operator mode is on. If not, turn it on.
  permanence =?[!pid].[!username].tmp off
  delete =?[!pid].[!username].tmp
  operator/l==?[!pid].[!username].tmp
  string [=?[!pid].[!username].tmp]
  delete =?[!pid].[!username].tmp
  [!equal,([!string]),(OFF)]
    OPERATOR/LABEL ON
  [!end]
  comment Operator mode is on -- proceed.
  class1 error
  class2 warning
  write
  [!equal,[!directory],:]
    [!equal,%0/I%,]
      write ** Full backup from directory [!DIRECTORY] at [!TIME] on [!DATE] **
    [!else]
      write ** Incremental backup from directory [!DIRECTORY] at [!TIME] on [!DATE] **
      string [=LAST_BACKUP]
      write
      write This backup will dump all files created or modified since [!string].
    [!end]
  [!else]
    write ** Backup from directory [!DIRECTORY] at [!TIME] on [!DATE] **
  [!end]
  write
  write Please insert the first diskette to receive backup material.
  write
  write This diskette and any others used for backup will be
  write overwritten -- so don't use diskettes that have material you
  write want to keep.
  write
  write Please number the paper label of each diskette as it is filled so
  write that -- if needed -- the diskettes can be restored in the correct order.
  write
  write ,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,  -- Beginning file backup --
  [!equal,[!directory],:]
    [!equal,%0/T%,]
      DUMP/RETAIN=0%0/V/L%[!nequal,%0/I%,]/AFTER/TLM=[!string][!end]&
	@LFD:VOL01:BACKUP    &
	    #\HELP\NET\PAGE\PATCH\PER\PROC\QUEUE\SWAP\SWAP.SWAP\SYSGEN&
\UTIL\?+.BRK\+.ED\?+.JOB\+.LS\?+.TMP   NET:NETGEN:+
    [!else]
      DUMP/RETAIN=0%0/V/L% @LFD:VOL01:BACKUP +
    [!end]
    write
    [!equal,%0/I%,]
      write ** Full backup of [!DIRECTORY] complete at [!TIME] **
    [!else]
      write ** Incremental backup of [!DIRECTORY] complete at [!TIME] **
    [!end]
    permanence/2=ignore  =LAST_BACKUP.BU  OFF
    delete/2=ignore  =LAST_BACKUP.BU
    rename/2=ignore  LAST_BACKUP  LAST_BACKUP.BU
    write/l==LAST_BACKUP   [!DATE]:[!TIME]

    write
    write This backup has created the file LAST_BACKUP in this directory
    write for future backups. Don't delete this file.
  [!else]
    DUMP/RETAIN=0%0/V/L%    @LFD:VOL01:BACKUP %1-%
    write
    write ** Backup of [!DIRECTORY] complete at [!TIME] **
  [!end]
[!end]
pop
